{
  "_comment": [
    "The TypeScript fixtures of the `dead-code-typescript` tool rule, as a project.",
    "ts-prune reads a tsconfig to build the module graph — 'exported and never",
    "imported' is a whole-project question, not a question about one loose file.",
    "`include` names this rule's two fixtures and nothing else, the same way",
    "`lib.rs` names only the Rust fixtures: the other TypeScript fixtures in this",
    "directory belong to eslint rules that read the paths they are given, and",
    "keeping them out of this program keeps one rule's fixtures from moving",
    "another rule's result."
  ],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2021",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  "include": ["dead-code-typescript.fail.ts", "dead-code-typescript.pass.ts"]
}
